WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.213
The split of authority is
the definition of the class.

2
00:00:03.213 --> 00:00:06.539
The partner is authoritative
for the person's affiliation,

3
00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:11.087
who works there and in what role, and for
the lifecycle of the credential it issues.

4
00:00:11.087 --> 00:00:15.248
The agency is authoritative for
everything that touches its systems:

5
00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:18.548
whether it trusts the partner's
identity service at all,

6
00:00:18.548 --> 00:00:21.847
which partner persons are
eligible, what they may reach,

7
00:00:21.847 --> 00:00:26.438
what assurance each transaction needs,
and when access is suspended or ended.

8
00:00:26.438 --> 00:00:27.801
One rule follows.

9
00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:32.238
No partner account gets access just
because it exists or synchronizes.

10
00:00:32.238 --> 00:00:35.875
An account in the tenant is a fact
about the partner's directory.

11
00:00:35.875 --> 00:00:42.170
Access is an agency decision, with an
approver, a sponsor, an expiry and evidence.
